'''vester''' (ves′tėr), ''n.'' One who invests money or other property; an investor. [Rare.]
{{smaller block|But in another of their papers . . . they declare that their ''vesters'' aim at nothing short of a community in land and in goods. {{right|''Southey'', To W. S. Landor, Aug. 22, 1829.}}}}

