'''vestment''' (vest′me̤nt), ''n.'' [Formerly also ''vestiment, vestament''; < ME. ''vestement'', < OF. ''vestement'', F. ''vêtement'' = Sp. ''vestimento'', m., ''vestimenta'', f., = Pg. ''vestimenta'' = It. ''vestimento'', m., ''vestimenta'', f., < L. ''vestimentum'', clothing, covering, < ''vestire'', clothe: see ''vest'', ''v.''] '''1.''' A covering or garment; some part of clothing or dress; an article of clothing; especially, some part of outer clothing; specifically, a ceremonial or official robe or garment.
{{smaller block|Hir ''vestiments'' which that they were.
{{right|''Chaucer'', Knight’s Tale, l. 2090.}}
The judges in their ''vestments'' of state attended to give advice on points of law.
{{right|''Macaulay'', Warren Hastings.}}}}
